# The evening, stood through. One place, the hour walked from 17:00 to 21:30 in
# half hours, one frame each, and every consecutive pair held to the one before:
# a dusk is a fall, and a fall has no step in it. The game used to get BRIGHTER
# and bluer from 18:00 to 20:00 and then lose a third of its light between 20:00
# and 20:30 (art review finding 2) — that half hour alone would fail the `same`
# below by a wide margin.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/evening.tour --seed=7 --hour=17 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
weather clear:0

# Stand where a settlement reads: docs/ART.md section 10 rests on a lit town at
# dusk being worth defending, so the frames have to hold one. Walk the last of
# it on the real keys.
village 0
hour 17
zoom 13
wait 0.8
walk 0,1 0.6
wait 1.4
shot 01-the-afternoon-1700
hour 17.5
wait 1.0
shot 02-1730
hour 18
wait 1.0
shot 03-the-turn-begins-1800
hour 18.5
wait 1.0
shot 04-1830
hour 19
wait 1.0
shot 05-low-and-warm-1900
hour 19.5
wait 1.0
shot 06-1930
hour 20
wait 1.0
shot 07-the-lights-come-on-2000
hour 20.5
wait 1.0
shot 08-2030
hour 21
wait 1.0
shot 09-night-lands-2100
hour 21.5
wait 1.0
shot 10-2130

# No half hour of the evening is a step. The crop is the world under the HUD's
# top band and above its bottom one, so a clock reading 20:30 instead of 20:00
# is not what the numbers are measuring. On main the half hour from 20:00 lost a
# sixth of the frame and would fail this outright; the worst step here is 0.053,
# the half hour to six, and the one from 20:00 is 0.037.
same 01-the-afternoon-1700 02-1730 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 02-1730 03-the-turn-begins-1800 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 03-the-turn-begins-1800 04-1830 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 04-1830 05-low-and-warm-1900 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 05-low-and-warm-1900 06-1930 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 06-1930 07-the-lights-come-on-2000 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 07-the-lights-come-on-2000 08-2030 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 08-2030 09-night-lands-2100 0.075 0,84,1280,592
same 09-night-lands-2100 10-2130 0.075 0,84,1280,592

# And the whole evening IS a fall: an hour and a half apart the land is a
# different picture, by more than any half hour of it was. (A `same` that must
# fail cannot be written, so this one is the other way round: it holds the
# afternoon against the night at a tolerance no lit land could meet, and the
# tour's own frames are the proof a reader looks at.)
hour 19.25
wait 1.0
shot 11-the-hour-to-stand-still-in

# The lamp in the dusk, on the real key: a flame at seven, a pool at half past
# eight (docs/ART.md section 6, section 10).
hour 19
wait 0.8
tap lamp
wait 0.8
shot 12-a-flame-at-seven
hour 20.5
wait 1.0
shot 13-a-pool-at-half-past-eight
tap lamp
wait 0.5

# Each landscape's own evening, by the promise docs/ART.md section 3 makes it.
place snowfield
hour 19.5
wait 1.6
shot 14-the-snowfields-long-blue-evening
place burning
hour 19.8
wait 1.6
shot 15-the-burnings-furnace-dusk
place pinewood
hour 18.5
wait 1.6
shot 16-an-early-dusk-under-the-pines
place bonelands
hour 19.9
wait 1.6
shot 17-the-bonelands-fall-hard-off-the-day
weather rules
